            <ArticleTitle>[Bilateral emphysematous pyelonephritis cured by medical therapy alone].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>174-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Emphysematous pyelonephritis is a necrotizing renal infection characterized by bacterial gas production in the renal and perirenal area. It is a rare infection diagnosed in diabetic patients in most cases. Emphysematous pyelonephritis has a high mortality rate. We herein report one case of bilateral emphysematous pyelonephritis managed by medical therapy alone.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
